<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">San Luis Potosí</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">San Luis <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/potosi">Potosí</a> is a state of north-central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, with a capital of the same name founded in 1592 after the discovery of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> nearby. Its eastern part lies in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huasteca">Huasteca</a>, home to Huastec and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nahuas">Nahua</a> communities. The state was an important mining and transport centre in colonial and modern times.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/san-luis-potosi.jpg" alt="San Luis Potosí" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Lucy Nieto · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cerro_del_Fraile_-_Matehuala,_San_Luis_Potos%C3%AD,_M%C3%A9xico.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
